---Compliance data for an OS policy
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.OSPolicyAssignmentReportOSPolicyCompliance
---@field osPolicyId? string The OS policy id
---@field complianceState? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.OSPolicyAssignmentReportOSPolicyComplianceComplianceStateEnum The compliance state of the OS policy.
---@field osPolicyResourceCompliances? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.OSPolicyAssignmentReportOSPolicyComplianceOSPolicyResourceComplianceList Compliance data for each resource within the policy that is applied to the VM.
---@field complianceStateReason? string The reason for the OS policy to be in an unknown compliance state. This field is always populated when `compliance_state` is `UNKNOWN`. If populated, the field can contain one of the following values: * `vm-not-running`: The VM was not running. * `os-policies-not-supported-by-agent`: The version of the OS Config agent running on the VM does not support running OS policies. * `no-agent-detected`: The OS Config agent is not detected for the VM. * `resource-execution-errors`: The OS Config agent encountered errors while executing one or more resources in the policy. See `os_policy_resource_compliances` for details. * `task-timeout`: The task sent to the agent to apply the policy timed out. * `unexpected-agent-state`: The OS Config agent did not report the final status of the task that attempted to apply the policy. Instead, the agent unexpectedly started working on a different task. This mostly happens when the agent or VM unexpectedly restarts while applying OS policies. * `internal-service-errors`: Internal service errors were encountered while attempting to apply the policy. * `os-policy-execution-pending`: OS policy was assigned to the given VM, but was not executed yet. Typically this is a transient condition that will go away after the next policy execution cycle.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.OSPolicyAssignmentReportOSPolicyComplianceComplianceStateEnum "UNKNOWN"|"COMPLIANT"|"NON_COMPLIANT"

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.OSPolicyAssignmentReportOSPolicyComplianceList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.OSPolicyAssignmentReportOSPolicyCompliance[]

---Compliance data for an OS policy resource.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.OSPolicyAssignmentReportOSPolicyComplianceOSPolicyResourceCompliance
---@field configSteps? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.OSPolicyAssignmentReportOSPolicyComplianceOSPolicyResourceComplianceOSPolicyResourceConfigStepList Ordered list of configuration completed by the agent for the OS policy resource.
