---A filter to target VM instances for patching. The targeted VMs must meet all criteria specified. So if both labels and zones are specified, the patch job targets only VMs with those labels and in those zones.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.PatchInstanceFilter
---@field zones? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringList Targets VM instances in ANY of these zones. Leave empty to target VM instances in any zone.
---@field all? boolean Target all VM instances in the project. If true, no other criteria is permitted.
---@field instanceNamePrefixes? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringList Targets VMs whose name starts with one of these prefixes. Similar to labels, this is another way to group VMs when targeting configs, for example prefix="prod-".
---@field groupLabels? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.PatchInstanceFilterGroupLabelList Targets VM instances matching ANY of these GroupLabels. This allows targeting of disparate groups of VM instances.
---@field instances? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringList Targets any of the VM instances specified. Instances are specified by their URI in the form `zones/[ZONE]/instances/[INSTANCE_NAME]`, `projects/[PROJECT_ID]/zones/[ZONE]/instances/[INSTANCE_NAME]`, or `https://www.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/[PROJECT_ID]/zones/[ZONE]/instances/[INSTANCE_NAME]`

---Targets a group of VM instances by using their [assigned labels](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/labeling-resources). Labels are key-value pairs. A `GroupLabel` is a combination of labels that is used to target VMs for a patch job. For example, a patch job can target VMs that have the following `GroupLabel`: `{"env":"test", "app":"web"}`. This means that the patch job is applied to VMs that have both the labels `env=test` and `app=web`.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.PatchInstanceFilterGroupLabel
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringMap Compute Engine instance labels that must be present for a VM instance to be targeted by this filter.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.PatchInstanceFilterGroupLabelList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.PatchInstanceFilterGroupLabel[]

