---Represents a time of day. The date and time zone are either not significant or are specified elsewhere. An API may choose to allow leap seconds. Related types are google.type.Date and `google.protobuf.Timestamp`.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.TimeOfDay
---@field minutes? number Minutes of an hour. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to 59.
---@field hours? number Hours of a day in 24 hour format. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and typically must be less than or equal to 23. An API may choose to allow the value "24:00:00" for scenarios like business closing time.
---@field nanos? number Fractions of seconds, in nanoseconds. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to 999,999,999.
---@field seconds? number Seconds of a minute. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and typically must be less than or equal to 59. An API may allow the value 60 if it allows leap-seconds.

---Represents a time zone from the [IANA Time Zone Database](https://www.iana.org/time-zones).
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.TimeZone
---@field id? string IANA Time Zone Database time zone. For example "America/New_York".
---@field version? string Optional. IANA Time Zone Database version number. For example "2019a".

---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.UpdateProjectFeatureSettingsProjectsLocationsGlobalRequest
---@field patchAndConfigFeatureSet? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.ProjectFeatureSettingsPatchAndConfigFeatureSetEnum|string Set PatchAndConfigFeatureSet for the project.
---@field name string Required. Immutable. Name specifies the URL for the ProjectFeatureSettings resource: projects/project_id/locations/global/projectFeatureSettings.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. Field mask that controls which fields of the ProjectFeatureSettings should be updated.

---This API resource represents the vulnerability report for a specified Compute Engine virtual machine (VM) instance at a given point in time. For more information, see [Vulnerability reports](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/os-inventory-management#vulnerability-reports).
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReport
---@field name? string Output only. The `vulnerabilityReport` API resource name. Format: `projects/{project_number}/locations/{location}/instances/{instance_id}/vulnerabilityReport`
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp for when the last vulnerability report was generated for the VM.
---@field vulnerabilities? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityList Output only. List of vulnerabilities affecting the VM.
---@field highestUpgradableCveSeverity? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportHighestUpgradableCveSeverityEnum Output only. Highest level of severity among all the upgradable vulnerabilities with CVEs attached.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportHighestUpgradableCveSeverityEnum "VULNERABILITY_SEVERITY_LEVEL_UNSPECIFIED"|"NONE"|"MINIMAL"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"CRITICAL"

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReport[]

---A vulnerability affecting the VM instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerability
---@field availableInventoryItemIds? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringList Corresponds to the `AVAILABLE_PACKAGE` inventory item on the VM. If the vulnerability report was not updated after the VM inventory update, these values might not display in VM inventory. If there is no available fix, the field is empty. The `inventory_item` value specifies the latest `SoftwarePackage` available to the VM that fixes the vulnerability.
---@field details? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityDetails Contains metadata as per the upstream feed of the operating system and NVD.
---@field updateTime? string The timestamp for when the vulnerability was last modified.
---@field installedInventoryItemIds? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringList Corresponds to the `INSTALLED_PACKAGE` inventory item on the VM. This field displays the inventory items affected by this vulnerability. If the vulnerability report was not updated after the VM inventory update, these values might not display in VM inventory. For some distros, this field may be empty.
---@field createTime? string The timestamp for when the vulnerability was first detected.
---@field items? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityItemList List of items affected by the vulnerability.

---Contains metadata information for the vulnerability. This information is collected from the upstream feed of the operating system.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityDetails
---@field severity? string Assigned severity/impact ranking from the distro.
---@field description? string The note or description describing the vulnerability from the distro.
---@field cvssV3? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.CVSSv3 The full description of the CVSSv3 for this vulnerability from NVD.
---@field references? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityDetailsReferenceList Corresponds to the references attached to the `VulnerabilityDetails`.
---@field cve? string The CVE of the vulnerability. CVE cannot be empty and the combination of should be unique across vulnerabilities for a VM.
---@field cvssV2Score? number The CVSS V2 score of this vulnerability. CVSS V2 score is on a scale of 0 - 10 where 0 indicates low severity and 10 indicates high severity.

---A reference for this vulnerability.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityDetailsReference
---@field source? string The source of the reference e.g. NVD.
---@field url? string The url of the reference.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityDetailsReferenceList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityDetailsReference[]

---OS inventory item that is affected by a vulnerability or fixed as a result of a vulnerability.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityItem
---@field installedInventoryItemId? string Corresponds to the `INSTALLED_PACKAGE` inventory item on the VM. This field displays the inventory items affected by this vulnerability. If the vulnerability report was not updated after the VM inventory update, these values might not display in VM inventory. For some operating systems, this field might be empty.
---@field upstreamFix? string The upstream OS patch, packages or KB that fixes the vulnerability.
---@field fixedCpeUri? string The recommended [CPE URI](https://cpe.mitre.org/specification/) update that contains a fix for this vulnerability.
---@field availableInventoryItemId? string Corresponds to the `AVAILABLE_PACKAGE` inventory item on the VM. If the vulnerability report was not updated after the VM inventory update, these values might not display in VM inventory. If there is no available fix, the field is empty. The `inventory_item` value specifies the latest `SoftwarePackage` available to the VM that fixes the vulnerability.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityItemList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityItem[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.VulnerabilityReportVulnerability[]

---Represents one week day in a month. An example is "the 4th Sunday".
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.WeekDayOfMonth
---@field weekOrdinal? number Required. Week number in a month. 1-4 indicates the 1st to 4th week of the month. -1 indicates the last week of the month.
---@field dayOffset? number Optional. Represents the number of days before or after the given week day of month that the patch deployment is scheduled for. For example if `week_ordinal` and `day_of_week` values point to the second Tuesday of the month and the `day_offset` value is set to `3`, patch deployment takes place three days after the second Tuesday of the month. If this value is negative, for example -5, patches are deployed five days before the second Tuesday of the month. Allowed values are in range [-30, 30].
---@field dayOfWeek? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.WeekDayOfMonthDayOfWeekEnum|string Required. A day of the week.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.WeekDayOfMonthDayOfWeekEnum "DAY_OF_WEEK_UNSPECIFIED"|"MONDAY"|"TUESDAY"|"WEDNESDAY"|"THURSDAY"|"FRIDAY"|"SATURDAY"|"SUNDAY"

---Represents a weekly schedule.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.WeeklySchedule
---@field dayOfWeek? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.WeeklyScheduleDayOfWeekEnum|string Required. Day of the week.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.WeeklyScheduleDayOfWeekEnum "DAY_OF_WEEK_UNSPECIFIED"|"MONDAY"|"TUESDAY"|"WEDNESDAY"|"THURSDAY"|"FRIDAY"|"SATURDAY"|"SUNDAY"

---Windows patching is performed using the Windows Update Agent.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.WindowsUpdateSettings
---@field exclusivePatches? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringList An exclusive list of kbs to be updated. These are the only patches that will be updated. This field must not be used with other patch configurations.
---@field excludes? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringList List of KBs to exclude from update.
---@field classifications? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.WindowsUpdateSettingsClassificationsItemEnumList Only apply updates of these windows update classifications. If empty, all updates are applied.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.WindowsUpdateSettingsClassificationsItemEnum "CLASSIFICATION_UNSPECIFIED"|"CRITICAL"|"SECURITY"|"DEFINITION"|"DRIVER"|"FEATURE_PACK"|"SERVICE_PACK"|"TOOL"|"UPDATE_ROLLUP"|"UPDATE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.WindowsUpdateSettingsClassificationsItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.WindowsUpdateSettingsClassificationsItemEnum|string)[]

---Yum patching is performed by executing `yum update`. Additional options can be set to control how this is executed. Note that not all settings are supported on all platforms.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.YumSettings
---@field security? boolean Adds the `--security` flag to `yum update`. Not supported on all platforms.
---@field excludes? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringList List of packages to exclude from update. These packages are excluded by using the yum `--exclude` flag.
---@field exclusivePackages? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringList An exclusive list of packages to be updated. These are the only packages that will be updated. If these packages are not installed, they will be ignored. This field must not be specified with any other patch configuration fields.
---@field minimal? boolean Will cause patch to run `yum update-minimal` instead.

---Zypper patching is performed by running `zypper patch`. See also https://en.opensuse.org/SDB:Zypper_manual.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.ZypperSettings
---@field withUpdate? boolean Adds the `--with-update` flag, to `zypper patch`.
---@field severities? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringList Install only patches with these severities. Common severities include critical, important, moderate, and low.
---@field withOptional? boolean Adds the `--with-optional` flag to `zypper patch`.
---@field exclusivePatches? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringList An exclusive list of patches to be updated. These are the only patches that will be installed using 'zypper patch patch:' command. This field must not be used with any other patch configuration fields.
---@field categories? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringList Install only patches with these categories. Common categories include security, recommended, and feature.
---@field excludes? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1.StringList List of patches to exclude from update.

